"engenn5le09ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "The Simple Past & Past Continuous Tenses", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Past Continuous tense to talk about something that was happening at a particular time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I was cooking <span class=\"strong\">when</span> you texted me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">While</span> I was swinging on the swing, it started to rain.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "My pants ripped <span class=\"strong\">as</span> I  fell.<br/> <br/> <br/>", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Form: subject + was/were + verb-ing</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use the Past Continuous tense together with the Simple Past tense. </br></br> The Past Continuous talks about a longer 'background' action.  </br></br>The Simple Past talks about a shorter event that happened in the middle of, or interrupted, the longer event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the words <span class=\"strong\">when, while</span> and <span class=\"strong\">as</span>.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Reacting to a Story", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "When someone tells you a story, it is important to react to show that you are listening. You can show surprise and interest.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Chelsea</span>: I fell into the sand!</br> <span class=\"strong\">Tom</span>: No way! What happened?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Show Surprise\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Show Interest \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">Oh?</br> Oh yeah?</br> Really?</br> Oh, really?</br> Is that right?</br> What happened?</br>  No way!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\